 "review": {
  "status": "unreviewed-fixture"
 },
 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1790). Words follow the Peters engraving's spelling and punctuation (the sisters' and officers' broken words with the print's ellipses, bell' idol as two words, all' anima on two notes, pifferi; with a semicolon). The first word sung, -fanno (bar 1, Fiordiligi and Dorabella), ends the sisters' Muojo d'affanno from the recitative before (Non v'è più tempo, amici), which shows and speaks that line whole, so it is left out of the phrases here. The chorus (bars 28–53, Bella vita militar sung again) has the same phrases as No. 8; its ids are ks, ka, kt and kb (sopranos, altos, tenors, basses), Ferrando's are r. IPA, word meanings and translations come from the app's reviewed Così libretto drafts (L16 and L17, IPA checked against Castel). IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
